Package: resolveR
Title: Predicting Sample Outcomes from Compositional Data
Version: 0.10.0
Authors@R:
    person("Gilles", "Colling", email = "gilles.colling051@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3070-6066"))
Description: Predict sample-level outcomes from compositional data (species
    lists, item sets, or any variable-length categorical input) with a neural
    network trained on a learned representation of each sample's composition.
    The composition can be encoded by feature hashing following Weinberger et
    al. (2009) <doi:10.1145/1553374.1553516>, by learned embeddings pooled
    over the sample, or by a transformer encoder following Vaswani et al.
    (2017) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1706.03762>, and regression and classification targets are
    fitted jointly with held-out evaluation, cross-validation and calibration
    diagnostics. The model is a C++ engine built on 'libtorch'. It is not
    compiled into this package: resolve.install_backend() fetches a prebuilt
    build into the user data directory on request, with optional graphics
    processing unit (GPU) acceleration through 'CUDA'.
